{"name": "n1_science_t2", "sha256": "5d4ddf73b04fa3640d7d14561fdf5120f8ad40cd479c9b4ce6ea5d9e1a008552", "words": 91, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 0.9999998807907104, "fraction_ai_assisted": 3.6478888486290995e-12, "fraction_human": 1.1060149063268909e-07, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "utc": "2026-10-23T02:44:56Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "High", 59, 0, 349, "Science circles the edges of consciousness, and here’s some of what it finds out there: people functioning with no felt controller, several things cognized at once, split-brain patients who can seem like two knowers sharing a skull, and one recent theory that models minds as nested parallel observers. The full nerdy tour is in the research report."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 31, 349, 530, " Science gives my argument a third wheel, making it safer to ride, but it will never show nibbāna itself – self and sense organs unweaving into self-presenting light flows of bliss."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 3, 530, 556, " That requires meditation."]]}
{"name": "n1_nde_t3", "sha256": "a56a806772aa48061298c19b859a32869ae7ab397cf24954e27125fb98f75012", "words": 99, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 0.8368580341339111, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.2338736387278906e-17, "fraction_human": 0.16314199566841125, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "utc": "2026-10-23T02:45:00Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "Low", 18, 0, 108, "The closest comparison that’s worth mentioning is the out-of-body perception in some near-death experiences."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 43, 108, 382, " People sometimes report seeing things from impossible angles, and a controversial subset of those reports were verified by others in the room (see this systematic analysis of near-death reports, the AWARE-II cardiac-arrest study, and a recent veridical-NDE evidence scale)."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 50, 382, 662, " Nobody could check anything like that in my room event, since I wasn’t floating around noticing specific details, so those reports don’t prove anything about mine. They might still help explain what I mean by an experience that wasn’t limited by the body’s vantage point anymore."]]}
{"name": "n1_burden_t3", "sha256": "57842ebc50670cb031a64a963524e4a2cc0284a66a84a044ca00464c4776f5d9", "words": 74, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 0.9999095797538757, "fraction_ai_assisted": 3.3196377504512986e-12, "fraction_human": 9.043572208611295e-05, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "utc": "2026-10-23T02:45:01Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "Medium", 24, 0, 124, "In SN 22.22 the five aggregates are the burden and craving is what picks it up, so the Buddha splits the accounting cleanly."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 21, 124, 234, " The tangle’s heavy by nature (even an arahant feels the first dart), and craving’s what keeps us carrying it."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 25, 234, 374, " And binding is literally heavy in physics too (quarks supply less than 1% of a proton’s mass, roughly 99% comes from gluon-binding energy)."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 9, 374, 435, " Matter weighs what its binding weighs. Light weighs nothing."]]}
{"name": "n1_diamond_t3", "sha256": "edba36ff26537230b4dd5301b089d4a341202898f2bb7b30c1941042e81b2f33", "words": 80, "headline": "AI Generated", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 1.0, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.0, "fraction_human": 7.989485809045682e-13, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "utc": "2026-10-23T02:45:03Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "Medium", 37, 0, 202, "I used to attribute “life is like a dream” directly to the historical Buddha, until I found out the famous stanza I loved comes from the later Mahāyāna Diamond Sutra, which puts some words in his mouth."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 44, 202, 436, " The early Pāli texts do have closely related images (SN 22.95 compares form to foam, feeling to a bubble, perception to a mirage and consciousness to a magic trick, and Dhammapada 170 asks us to see the world as a bubble and mirage)."]]}
{"name": "n1_driving_t3", "sha256": "62289f1896ab71d3b51488654f554b3bf510577b539183807c678bc15495f4ee", "words": 86, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 0.9678038358688354, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.03217513486742973, "fraction_human": 2.1028550690971315e-05, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "utc": "2026-10-23T02:45:05Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "Low", 24, 0, 133, "My buddy E. told me he had much stronger episodes while driving: for long stretches, his own car and the traffic seemed to disappear."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 6, 133, 166, " He never had an accident either."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 22, 166, 298, " God only knows why (luck, a misunderstanding of what was happening, something about how these states work, some mix of those, etc)."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 31, 298, 474, "\nEither way, I wouldn’t keep driving through that myself. If you’re having episodes like that, I’d stay away from driving or running machinery until you understand them better."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 6, 474, 503, " That’s my own CYA showing. 😇"]]}
